\includegraphics[width=0.49\textwidth]{Figure_002-b.pdf}
\caption{Distributions of the dimuon invariant mass between 2.8 and 3.4\GeV~(left) and of the \pt of the \PJGy meson candidate~(right). Processes are normalized to their theoretical cross sections. The simulation assumes a value of $m_\PQt=172.5\GeV$. The lower panel shows the ratio of the number of events observed in data to the number expected from simulation. One point is not visible in the lower panel of  the right plot, as it would require to enlarge the $y$-axis range up to 3.5 units.}
\label{fig:jpsi}
\end{figure}

The invariant mass, $m_{\PJGy+\ell}$, is computed from the combination of the \PJGy meson candidate and the leading lepton. The distributions are shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:jpsil}.

